  "title": "Kerr shadow outline vs Bardeen (1973)",
  "description": "Parallel rays from a plane 1e6 M away, at inclination i from the spin axis. Along the line from the outline's centre through each point (alpha, beta) of Bardeen's analytic edge, the capture boundary is found by bisection on ray fate; the deviation is its distance from Bardeen's point, in M (positive = traced edge outside). Starting at finite distance costs little here: light reaching a distant observer travels along the outgoing principal null direction l of the Kerr-Schild form g = eta + f l l, so the f l l correction to the initial momentum is of order (b / D)^2 ~ 1e-11.",
